      "title": "Posture and Alignment",
      "detail": "Maintain a tall, upright posture with your ears, shoulders, hips, and ankles in alignment. This will help to reduce your center of gravity and improve your balance and stability."
    },
    {
      "title": "Foot Strike and Stride",
      "detail": "Land midfoot or forefoot instead of heel striking, and aim for a smooth, efficient stride. Try to strike the ground with the ball of your foot, and then roll forward onto your toes."
    },
    {
      "title": "Cadence and Stride Rate",
      "detail": "Focus on quick turnover and a high cadence (around 160-170 steps per minute). This will help you to maintain a consistent pace and reduce your risk of overuse injuries."
    },
    {
      "title": "Arm Swing and Hand Position",
      "detail": "Keep your arms relaxed and bent at around a 90-degree angle. Your hands should be in a loose fist, with your wrists cocked slightly upward. Avoid crossing your arms over your body or holding them too far away from your body."
    },
    {
      "title": "Breathing and Core Engagement",
      "detail": "Practice deep, rhythmic breathing to help you relax and maintain a consistent pace. Engage your core muscles to support your posture and stability, and avoid tensing up or holding your breath."
