{
  "plan": {
    "overview": "Creating a weekly meal plan on a budget requires some planning and organization, but it can be a great way to save money and eat healthy. By planning your meals in advance, you can avoid last-minute takeout or dining out, which can be expensive. You can also make sure you're using up all the ingredients you buy and reducing food waste.",
    "rationale": "By creating a weekly meal plan on a budget, you can save money on food expenses, reduce food waste, and eat healthier. You can also reduce stress and save time by having a plan in place for the week."
  },
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Step 1: Plan Your Meals",
      "detail": "Start by planning out your meals for the week. Think about what you like to eat and what you have in your pantry and fridge. You can also look up recipes online or use a meal planning app to get inspiration. Make a list of the meals you want to make and the ingredients you'll need."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 2: Make a Grocery List",
      "detail": "Once you have your meal plan, make a list of the ingredients you'll need to buy. Try to stick to what you already have at home and avoid buying too much of anything. You can also use a grocery list app to help you keep track of what you need to buy."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 3: Shop Smart",
      "detail": "When you're at the grocery store, try to shop smart. Look for sales and discounts on the ingredients you need. Buy in bulk if you can, and avoid buying pre-packaged or processed foods. You can also use cashback apps or rewards programs to earn money back on your groceries."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 4: Cook and Prep",
      "detail": "Once you have your groceries, start cooking and prepping your meals. Try to cook in bulk and use leftovers to reduce food waste. You can also prep ingredients like vegetables or grains in advance to make cooking easier."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 5: Review and Adjust",
      "detail": "At the end of the week, review your meal plan and see how it went. Did you stick to your plan? Were there any meals you didn't like? Use this information to adjust your plan for the next week and make it even better."
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Creating a weekly meal plan on a budget requires some planning and organization, but it can be a great way to save money and eat healthy. By following these steps, you can make a plan that works for you and your budget, and enjoy the benefits of meal planning for weeks to come."
}

{
